{"content":[{"c":["AVENGER OF BLOOD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Person who performed the duty of pursuing and ultimately executing the murderer of a close relative (",{"href":"?bref=Num.35.1-34","r":"Num.35.1-34","rawR":"Num.35.1-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.35.1-34","value":"Num.35.1-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 35"},"). Such a “redeemer” was expected to act in instances of deliberate murder but not of accidental manslaughter. A person guilty of manslaughter could find asylum in any one of six designated cities throughout the land (",{"href":"?bref=Num.35.11","r":"Num.35.11","rawR":"Num.35.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.35.11","value":"Num.35.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"35:11"},") so that regular judicial processes could be set in motion. The avenger of blood can be seen in the accounts of Gideon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.18-21","r":"Judg.8.18-21","rawR":"Judg.8.18-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.18-21","value":"Judg.8.18-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:18-21"},"), Joab (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.3.27,30","r":"2Sam.3.27,30","rawR":"2Sam.3.27,30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.3.27,30","value":"2Sam.3.27,30"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 3:27, 30"},"), the Gibeonites (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.21.1-22","r":"2Sam.21.1-22","rawR":"2Sam.21.1-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.21.1-22","value":"2Sam.21.1-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 21"},"), and Amaziah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.14.5-6","r":"2Kgs.14.5-6","rawR":"2Kgs.14.5-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.14.5-6","value":"2Kgs.14.5-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 14:5-6"},"). During the monarchy the king could evidently thwart the avenger (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.14.8-11","r":"2Sam.14.8-11","rawR":"2Sam.14.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.14.8-11","value":"2Sam.14.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 14:8-11"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The custom was rooted in the ordinance of God that required a life for a life in any case of intentional homicide (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.9.6","r":"Gen.9.6","rawR":"Gen.9.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.9.6","value":"Gen.9.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 9:6"},"). Unfortunately, the intent of the law—to impress upon humanity the sacredness of human life—has sometimes been greatly distorted, leading to blood feuds and the annihilation of whole families in some societies."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Civil Law and Justice"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AvengerofBlood","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.35.1-34","rawQueryValue":"Num.35.1-34","sourceRefExact":"Num.35.1-34"},{"anchorText":"35:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.35.11","rawQueryValue":"Num.35.11","sourceRefExact":"Num.35.11"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:18-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.18-21","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.18-21","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.18-21"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 3:27, 30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.3.27,30","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.3.27,30","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.3.27,30"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.21.1-22","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.21.1-22","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.21.1-22"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 14:5-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.14.5-6","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.14.5-6","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.14.5-6"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 14:8-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.14.8-11","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.14.8-11","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.14.8-11"},{"anchorText":"Gn 9:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.9.6","rawQueryValue":"Gen.9.6","sourceRefExact":"Gen.9.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"af205b0edd72a36d6cad236a403f6b0e445b627f5b08bf6634b808492ede12dc","sourceItemName":"AvengerofBlood","sourceItemOrder":625,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AvengerofBlood","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Avenger of Blood","title":"Avenger of Blood","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}